---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Source Methodology — Formation.Legal"
  description="How Formation.Legal researches, verifies, and updates its guides and tools for non-US founders."
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <div class="mb-10 border-b border-[var(--color-border)] pb-8">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-[var(--color-text-primary)] sm:text-4xl">Source Methodology</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 text-lg text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">Last updated: April 2026</p>
    </div>

    <div class="prose prose-lg">
      <p>
        Formation.Legal produces decision-support content for non-US founders. Every guide, provider review, and tool recommendation follows a structured research methodology designed for accuracy, transparency, and operational relevance.
      </p>

      <h2>1. Primary Source Priority</h2>
      <p>
        We prioritize official, primary sources over secondary commentary:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>State statutes and Secretary of State websites</strong> for entity formation rules.</li>
        <li><strong>IRS publications and instructions</strong> for tax obligations (Form 5472, EIN requirements, etc.).</li>
        <li><strong>FinCEN rulings</strong> for BOI reporting requirements.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment processor documentation</strong> (Stripe Atlas docs, PayPal business policies) for eligibility criteria.</li>
        <li><strong>Bank compliance disclosures</strong> for account opening requirements.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Provider Testing</h2>
      <p>
        Where feasible, we test formation providers directly. We document the actual process, timeline, and outcome rather than relying solely on marketing materials. Provider reviews marked with a "Tested" badge indicate first-hand experience.
      </p>

      <h2>3. Community Data Points</h2>
      <p>
        US business formation for non-residents involves rapidly changing policies (especially around banking and payment processor approvals). We supplement our primary research with anonymized community data points from founder forums, immigration attorney insights, and CPA consultations.
      </p>

      <h2>4. Update Cadence</h2>
      <p>
        Every guide includes a visible "Last Reviewed" date. Our target review cadence is:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>High-impact guides</strong> (Stripe access, banking): Quarterly review.</li>
        <li><strong>Compliance guides</strong> (annual filings, BOI): Updated within 30 days of regulatory changes.</li>
        <li><strong>Provider reviews</strong>: Updated when pricing, services, or policies change materially.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. What We Do Not Do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We do not guarantee outcomes. Banking approvals, Stripe access, and compliance depend on your specific situation.</li>
        <li>We do not provide legal, tax, or financial advice. See our <a href="/disclaimer">Disclaimer</a>.</li>
        <li>We do not accept payment from providers to alter research findings.</li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        If you believe any of our research is inaccurate or outdated, please contact our editorial team. We take corrections seriously and will update published content promptly.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
